=== PARITY (vs web shared/WidgetFlowDiagram.tsx) ===
  Nature → the web component is PURE PRESENTATIONAL (props: nodes, arrows, compact, emptyMessage; no
    hooks, no t() calls, no charts/maps). The native primitive is likewise presentational: consumers
    pass a resolved WidgetFlowGraph (or a render state). NO HTTP, NO data source invented (would violate
    parity). "Data sources: (none)" honored exactly.
  Model → FlowNode {id,label,value,formattedValue,icon→symbol,position} and FlowArrow {from,to,value,
    active,color→tint} are 1:1 ports of the web interfaces. POSITION_COORDS reproduced verbatim
    (top 50,12 · bottom 50,88 · left 12,50 · right 88,50 · center 50,50) — unit-tested.
  Geometry → WidgetFlowBuilder.segment offsets both ends by the node radius so lines never overlap the
    rings (web x1=cx+ux*r … x2=cx-ux*r); NODE_RADIUS 14 / compact 10; stroke 1..4 scaled by
    |value|/max(|value|,1) (web strokeForValue) — unit-tested (vertical + horizontal edges, guard).
  Visibility → compact keeps the 3 largest arrows by |value| and truncates labels >3 chars to the first
    3 upper-cased (web visibleArrows + label slice) — unit-tested.
  Color → arrowColor(value, tint): explicit tint override, else value>0 emerald-400, <0 red-400, else
    muted token (web arrowColor) — unit-tested. Node chrome fill-white/5 → textPrimary@5%, stroke-white/20
    → border token, label fill-white/60 → muted token (theme-safe).
  Animation → active arrows dash "4 8" with a marching offset (web dashFlow keyframe → -12 over 0.8s),
    drawn in a Canvas inside TimelineView(.animation(paused: reduceMotion)); the node value rolls via
    contentTransition(.numericText()) (web AnimatedNumber), snapping under Reduce Motion. SVG
    <line>/<circle>/<foreignObject> → Canvas stroke + positioned SwiftUI views (crisp SF Symbols).
  Empty → web nodes.length===0 → EmptyState("No flow data available"); native maps to ContentUnavailable
    (the component TSEmptyState wraps) driven by the per-surface facade, default emptyMessage overridable.
  Shared comps → web data-display(AnimatedNumber) → WidgetFlowValueText (numericText roll);
    web feedback(EmptyState) → ContentUnavailableView/TSEmptyState equivalent.

=== STATES (all render — no hidden surfaces) ===
  loading  → skeleton chrome (TSSkeleton) + a11y label.
  content  → the diagram (web's own branch).
  empty    → ContentUnavailableView with the (overridable) "No flow data available" message + hint.
  error    → triangle + title + optional detail + Retry affordance (onRetry), a11y-combined.
  stale    → cached diagram + amber "Reconnecting — values may be stale" chip + AUTO-refresh (onRefresh,
             cancelled on state change) + manual refresh button.
  offline  → cached diagram + muted "Offline — showing last known values" chip + refresh button.
  Each state has a #if DEBUG preview; the content/empty/state-mapping logic is unit-tested.

